# The core release every cluster must be able to roll forward from: ci-checks.yml's
# `Upgrade path` job starts a cluster on this release's published merod, writes data,
# rolls it onto the PR's merod as mdma rolls a Calimero Cloud cluster, and reads it back
# (crates/node/tests/fault/upgrade_path.py; docs: contribute/testing, "Upgrade path").
#
# Keep it at the latest published release: once a release's GitHub assets are up,
# set this to its tag (at the latest in the next release PR; CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Cutting a release"). The job warns when a newer release exists.
#
# A change that cannot keep old data readable and ships no migration is a hard
# cutover: replace the version line with `hard-cutover: <PR> <why>` in that PR, mark
# it in CHANGELOG.md, and add it to mdma's release_compat CUTOVERS. The job then
# reports the cutover instead of running, until the next release puts a version back.
1.0.0-rc.21
